  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have a project with about four or five worlds in it, separated into different scenes. I've been investigating why my scenes have such high filesizes despite using compression methods and have found within the editor log that the VRCSDK is uploading not just the files for the scene I'm uploading, but also that of an entirely unrelated scene that shares no content with this one. I can also see that it's building from it when I hit the build and upload button, starting with the unrelated scene and then showing my current scene as part 2 of the build process. Is this a bug, or perhaps user error? If it is an error on my part, what can be done to correct this? (At the moment I've removed the unrelated scene and its files from my project)",
